# Key Insights

## 1. Category Performance

- Geopolitics & War was the strongest-performing category in the analysis.
- It generated around 5.19Cr total views across 21 videos.
- Business & Entrepreneurship had 13 videos, but around 60% of them performed below the channel average.
- This shows that the topic of the conversation can have a major impact on video performance.

## 2. Upload Day Analysis

- Thursday had the highest average views among the different upload days.
- This suggests that Thursday could be a good day to test new uploads.
- However, upload day alone does not determine performance; topic and guest selection also matter.

## 3. Video Duration

- Videos longer than 30 minutes recorded the highest average engagement rate.
- Their average engagement rate was around 2.69%.
- This suggests that longer conversations can still perform well when the content keeps viewers engaged.

## 4. Views & Engagement

- Views and engagement showed a positive relationship, but the relationship was not very strong.
- This means a video can get high views without necessarily having the highest engagement.
- Looking at both views and engagement gives a better understanding of content performance.

## 5. Main Takeaway

The analysis suggests that **topic, guest selection and content quality** are more important than simply uploading more videos.

For future content, the channel can:

→ Experiment more with high-performing topics.

→ Test Thursday uploads.

→ Continue long-form conversations when the topic has strong audience interest.

→ Track both views and engagement to understand content quality.
